With this information, we can now create assertions for every new entry into the code. The "Debug.Assert" statements are placed immediately after the lines of code that introduce the new entry.--------------------```cs
using Debug = System.Diagnostics.Debug;

namespace ArrayList.Test
{
    public partial class ArrayListContractTest
    {
        public void PUT_InsertContract([PexAssumeUnderTest]ArrayList arrList, int x, int index)
        {
            AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(index <= arrList.Count && index >= 0);
            
            int Old_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
            int Old_x = x;
            int Old_index = index;
            int Old_arrListIndexOfX = arrList.IndexOf(x);
            int Old_arrListLastIndexOfX = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);
            bool Old_arrListContainsX = arrList.Contains(x);

            arrList.Insert(index, x);

            int New_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
            int New_arrListIndexOfX = arrList.IndexOf(x);
            int New_arrListLastIndexOfX = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);
            bool New_arrListContainsX = arrList.Contains(x);

            // debug assert start
            Debug.Assert(Old_arrListIndexOfX >= -1, "position of x is not valid (Old_arrListIndexOfX)");
            
            // Output the assert statements only by removing this block
            // This block for generating the assert statements with values
            {
                Debug.Assert(Old_arrListCount == New_arrListCount, "Counts are not matching.");
                Debug.Assert(Old_x == x, "Value should not change.");
                Debug.Assert(Old_index == index, "Index should not change.");
                Debug.Assert(Old_arrListIndexOfX == New_arrListIndexOfX, "IndexOf x should not change.");
                Debug.Assert(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX == New_arrListLastIndexOfX, "LastIndexOf x should not change.");
                Debug.Assert(Old_arrListContainsX == New_arrListContainsX, "Contains x should not change.");
            }
            // end of assert block
        }
    }
}
```

Please replace `ArrayList` with the actual class in your project. Also, take care, the code is written assuming your `ArrayList` class has `IndexOf` and `LastIndexOf` methods. In C#, `List.IndexOf` and `List.LastIndexOf` return -1 if the item was not found. So, "Old_arrListIndexOfX >= -1" may not provide the expected output, you need to modify it based on your class behaviors.--------------------Here are the output assert statements for the comments in your C# code:

